1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Study Coach turns saved notes
into explanations and practice.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
This is the working Rust application,
with a browser workspace.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Notes and history stay on this computer.
Asking sends source text to a provider.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The comparison used the same 50 cases.
Each new configuration ran once.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The baseline scored 78%.
The revised prompt scored 86%.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Retrieval also scored 86%, using
36.03% fewer mean input tokens.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Find the Test scope source
in the source panel.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The source panel exposes the notes
available for answering.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
An exact quotation must match
an original source passage.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Bring the original source passage
into view before asking.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Ask: How does a unit test differ
from an integration test?

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
This question uses the same
Rust core as the evaluator.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Ask Study Coach to send this question
to the selected Groq 120B model.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Wait for the provider response.
This is a real model request.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The response now includes an explanation
and source evidence.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Read the explanation alongside
the source quotation.

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The app checks that each quotation
appears in its named source.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
An exact quote is checkable evidence.
It does not prove every answer claim.

19
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Next, test unclear input:
three question marks.

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Try three question marks
instead of a meaningful study question.

21
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
An unclear question needs guidance
before a source based answer.

22
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
For punctuation only input,
a local clarification is enough.

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The app asks for a clearer question.
No model request is needed.

24
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Open My notes to add original material
to the local source library.

25
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Give the new source a title
and paste the short test scope passage.

26
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Save Demo notes to make this source
available for the next question.

27
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
The saved source now has a stable ID
in the local library.

28
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Open Past questions to revisit
an earlier accepted answer.

29
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
History keeps the question, response,
and evidence on this computer.

30
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Choose the saved question
to restore its explanation and evidence.

31
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
The saved answer returns without
another model request.

32
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Connections lets users choose a model
and enter their own provider keys.

33
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
The key fields stay blank on this screen.
Saved keys are not returned here.

34
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Groq and NVIDIA offer limited free access.
There is no automatic paid fallback.

35
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Return to Study to keep learning
from the saved notes.

36
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
One run on visible development cases.
These results do not measure learning.